        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1b7a865e-e747-5cb4-9867-a61c328a386d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jefferson Davis, Alexander H. Stephens, Franklin Pierce\n- Roles: President of the Confederate States, Vice President of the Confederate States, United States Secretary of War\n- Places: White House of the Confederacy\n- Concepts: Provisional Confederate States Constitution, Confederate States of America\n\nFacts:\n- The White House of the Confederacy was built in 1818.\n- Jefferson Davis served as the 23rd United States Secretary of War under U.S. President Franklin Pierce from 1853 to 1857.\n- Jefferson Davis and Alexander H. Stephens had been elected President and Vice President under the Provisional Confederate States Constitution before their later permanent election.\n- Jefferson Davis and Alexander H. Stephens were elected as the first permanent President and Vice President of the Confederate States of America for six-year terms running from February 22, 1862, to February 22, 1868.\n- The White House of the Confederacy was the main executive residence of Jefferson Davis from August 1861 until April 1865.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
